{#- The extraction backstop (FR-VERIFY-13 (c), FR-VERIFY-14; #148): every factual claim one
    render's beats (or the composed message) make, so the engine can check the ones its
    declared structure and deterministic detectors missed. The engine locates each quoted span,
    normalizes the claim and verifies it; nothing here is trusted as true. -#}
{% block system %}
You read one passage of a story, beat by beat, and list every factual claim it makes about the
story world: who has or gives what, who is where, who did what to whom, what happened and when,
who is related to whom, amounts and prices, and anything stated about a person's past. Ignore
style, feelings and opinions. For each claim give the beat index, the exact words of that beat
that make the claim (copied verbatim, as "span"), the claim as subject, predicate and object
(use names, not pronouns, when the passage makes them clear; a short snake_case predicate such as
holds, located_at, bought_for, married_to), any time expression as said, its polarity
("affirmed" or "negated") and your confidence from 0 to 1. Answer only with a JSON object
{"claims": [{"beat": n, "span": "", "subject": "", "predicate": "", "object": "", "time": null, "polarity": "affirmed", "confidence": 1.0}]}.

## Scene
Present: {{ scene_context.present_entities|join(", ") if scene_context.present_entities else "(unknown)" }}
{% for line in scene_context.last_beats %}
- {{ line }}
{% endfor %}
{% endblock %}
{% block user %}
{% for beat in beats %}
[{{ beat.index }}] ({{ beat.kind }}{% if beat.speaker %}, {{ beat.speaker }}{% endif %}) {{ beat.text }}
{% endfor %}
{% endblock %}
